cient Greek","termine":"γράμμα","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Uncertain. Either: * a variant of gërmih, * a denominative verb derived from gërmë (“letter”) in its otherwise unattested meaning 'line, scratch'; it would have originally meant 'to scratch lines', and thus from Ancient Greek γράμμα (grámma)."},{"parola":"gërshet","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"alternatively","significato":"plait, braid","termine_origine":"κορσωτός","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"κορσωτός","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From gër- + *shet, the latter a variant of shat. More at shat. Alternatively, from Ancient Greek κορσωτός (korsōtós)"},{"parola":"halinos","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Unknown","significato":"to corrupt","termine_origine":"χαλινός","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"χαλινός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Unknown. Maybe related to hall. Some suggest a borrowing from Ancient Greek χαλινός (khalinós) \"bridle\", with a complicated semantic development from \"bridle\" to \"to stop\" to \"obstruct, prevent\" to \"corrupt\""},{"parola":"hjima","pos":"adv","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"down, under","termine_origine":"χαμαί","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"χαμαί","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Probably from Ancient Greek χαμαί (khamaí)."},{"parola":"hutë","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"vulture","termine_origine":"ὦτος","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ὦτος","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"ōtus","categoria":"latinismo_dot